title: Keep chain-selection notified when a coalesced approval is only partly valid

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      `import_approval` processes every candidate named in a coalesced
      `ImportApproval` in one loop, writing overlay state and accumulating
      actions as it goes. A later per-candidate failure (typically
      `NoAssignment`) used to `respond_early!` with an empty action list,
      discarding `Action::NoteApprovedInChainSelection` even though the
      overlay already marked the block fully approved.

      Approval-distribution rejects a coalesced vote as soon as any named
      candidate has no known assignment, so this path is not reached from
      the network. GRANDPA uses `ApprovedAncestor` and does not depend on
      `ChainSelectionMessage::Approved`. The import change is a defensive
      check against that early return.

      Per-candidate errors now skip that candidate and continue. Accumulated
      actions are always returned. The overall result remains `Bad` if any
      named candidate failed.

  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      Hardens coalesced approval import so a per-candidate failure keeps
      actions already accumulated for the valid candidates.
      Approval-distribution already rejects a vote that names an unassigned
      candidate, and GRANDPA finality does not use this notification, so
      live chain behavior is unchanged. No CLI, config, or migration
      changes.

crates:
  - name: polkadot-node-core-approval-voting
    bump: patch
